##  (-) Characters to escape: %, $
## 
##  Min  Hour Day  Mon  Weekday
##  *    *    *    *    *    [user]   [command to be executed]
##  ┬    ┬    ┬    ┬    ┬
##  │    │    │    │    └─  Weekday  (0=Sun .. 6=Sat)
##  │    │    │    └──────  Month    (1..12)
##  │    │    └───────────  Day      (1..31)
##  │    └────────────────  Hour     (0..23)
##  └─────────────────────  Minute   (0..59)
## 
##--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Run the scraper hourly, 20 min past the hour. The user field is root, so the root shell
# opens /proc/1/fd/1 (the container log, as in backup_service); the scraper itself runs as
# dockeruser through as-dockeruser (it refuses root).
20 * * * * root /usr/local/bin/as-dockeruser /usr/local/bin/python /app/flexgate_scraper.py > /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1

# cron.d scripts must specify the user to run the command
# cron.d scripts must have a blank line (or comment) at the end
# cron.d scripts must not contain . or - in the filename (no extension!)
# cron.d scripts must be placed in /etc/cron.d/
# cron.d scripts must be owned by root and have permissions 644 (rw-r--r--)
# cron.d scripts do not have access to environment variables set by docker compose